> @Fabian-K Until you handle the request by calling `route.continue()`, `route.abort()`, `route.fulfill()` or `route.fallback()`, the request is "pending". Here is an example of slowing down each request for 3 seconds:
> 
> ```ts
> await page.route('**/*', async route => {
> await page.waitForTimeout(3000);
